aeat_party_validation
=====================

The aeat_party_validation module of the Tryton application platform.

Installing
----------

See INSTALL

Configuration
-------------

Load the certificate and private key with certificate_manager, then select
the AEAT Certificate in Parties > Configuration for each company.
The certificate_manager encryption and production settings apply.
The legacy account_es_sii certificate and privatekey settings are no longer used.

Validation
----------

The wizard checks each active Spanish identifier and records its last AEAT
check in party.identifier.aeat_validated_at. aeat_valid is true
only for Identificado (case-insensitive); similar, deregistered, revoked,
unprocessed and unknown results are not a positive validation. Updating names
from the wizard checks the new names again. Changing the party name clears the
validation of all its identifiers. Changing an identifier code, type, owner or
active state clears its own validation. Copies must also be validated again.

The supported identifier types are es_cif (legal entities), es_dni (DNI with
its check letter), es_nie and es_vat. They are sent as the Spanish NIF of nine
characters, without an ES prefix. eu_vat is supported only when starting with
ES; this prefix is removed for the request. Foreign EU VAT identifiers and
es_cae (an activity and establishment code, not a NIF) are not checked.

